cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data, code or framework, please cite it as below."
title: "The Championship Cube: A Six-Face Diagnostic Framework for Evaluating NBA Championship Contention"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ChampionshipCube-Sloan2027"
abstract: >-
  Data, analysis code and a prototype diagnostic (KIRIN) for the Championship Cube, a six-face
  framework (Team, Player, Coach, Front Office, Controllable External and Uncontrollable External)
  applied to 37 matched NBA champion / Finals runner-up pairs, 1989-90 to 2025-26. Team and Player
  Faces are statistically tested; Coach Face and two Front Office proxies show no effect; the
  organisational faces are an unvalidated single-coder pilot. Submitted to the MIT Sloan Sports
  Analytics Conference (SSAC) 2027.
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChampionshipCube-Sloan2027/The-Championship-Cube-A-Front-Office-Framework-for-Building-NBA-Champions"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - NBA
  - basketball analytics
  - championship contention
  - matched-pair analysis
  - front office
  - sports analytics
date-released: 2026-09-29
